{
  "esm": "1.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "WRFWeselySurfaceResistance",
    "description": "Surface (canopy) resistance Rc of WRF-Chem's dry-deposition scheme, SUBROUTINE rc of chem/module_dep_simple.F (WRF v4.8.0), for every gas on a species axis at ONE surface state.\n\nThis is a NEW component, not a repair of components/atmospheric_deposition/wesley_dry_gas.esm. That one is a migration of AtmosphericDeposition.jl -- the Wesely (1989) PAPER plus Walmsley & Wesely (1996), over the 11 Wesely land-use categories, with a GEOS-Chem species list -- and WRF's code is a different scheme wearing the same name. Audited against the running model, all 19 overlapping species differ on at least one constant (H2O2's H* by a factor of 671, acetic acid by 235, cresol by 952, and PAN, glyoxal, methylglyoxal and acetic acid have f0 flipped between 0 and 1), it has no dhr temperature correction at all, no Erisman branches, an Rc ceiling of 9999 s/m where WRF has none, and it covers 19 of the 38 gases WRF deposits. Bolting WRF-derived tests onto it would simply have made them red.\n\nFour paths, selected by the gas index. The GENERAL path is Wesely's four parallel resistances with the ground one in series with rac. OZONE differs by using rclo/rgso directly, substituting rluo1/rluo2 outright under dew or rain, and capping rac at 100 s/m. SO2 and NH3 are wholesale ERISMAN ET AL. (1994) replacements: SO2's cuticle resistance is a function of relative humidity, its combination has only three terms and no rac at all, and it collapses to the bare ground resistance over snow, urban/desert soil, water or ice; NH3 bypasses H* and f0 entirely and is read off a table of land class, season, day/night, wetness and temperature. A gas with hstar = 0 never enters the loop and keeps Rc = 1.\n\n`srfres` is what wesely_driver actually passes on, which is Rc except that the last two gas slots -- HO and HO2 for RADM2 -- are zeroed outright so they deposit at the aerodynamic limit.\n\nSCOPE OF THE TESTS, stated plainly. The reference column visits exactly ONE (iland, iseason) pair and never wets the surface: julday 295 puts every call in iseason 2, ivgtyp 2 maps to iland 2, and rhchem never reaches 95 nor is there rain. So the tests below, 7 meteorological states x 43 gases, pin the general path, the O3 path and the dry branches of SO2 and NH3 thoroughly and the wet, rain, snow and other-land-use branches not at all. In particular FORTRAN_BUGS B4 -- the factor-9 disagreement between the two spellings of the cuticle conductance -- lives in the wet branch and is NOT exercised here. A regime sweep that reaches those branches is the next step.\n\nSPECIES AXIS (2026-11-12). The surface state (iland, iseason, T, rad, rh and the wet/rain/high-NH3 flags) and everything built from it alone -- the land-use table reads, rs, rdc, resice, the O3 and SO2 paths -- are shared by every gas, as rc() computes them for one column; the gas index `igas` is per species, and with it the four species constants (looked up by `igas[s]`), the general path (hstary through rc_general), the path selection `rc` and `srfres`. The NH3 class cascade is per species too, but only because its fall-through branch is the species' own rc_general; `rc` reads it at the species whose igas is NH3. The per-species arithmetic is written as plain arithmetic on the [spc] arrays (name-aligned broadcast, esm-spec 4.3.4), so it reads as the one-gas formulas; only the table lookups and the igas-dependent selections index the axis explicitly. A consumer binds NSPEC at the mount edge and supplies `igas` as an [spc] array; the [spc] `srfres` is what WRFWeselyDepositionVelocity.srfres takes. This component's own tests use NSPEC = 10: each ESM_SWEEP regime is one test of its ten gases, and each in-model call's 43 gas slots are five tests of ten (the last test is the call's last ten slots and asserts only the three not already asserted). 1642 assertions, unchanged in number from the one-gas tests they regroup. Deliberately broken on 2026-11-12, each caught: every species reading hstar at igas[1] (1187 fail), dratio looked up in reversed species order (372), every general-path species reading rc_general[1] (1167), srfres reading rc[1] (259). Reading rc_nh3[1] at the NH3 species is NOT caught, and cannot be with these regimes: the only reachable fall-through (season 4 on grass or agricultural land) lands on the 1 s/m floor for NH3 and for species 1 (SO2) alike."
  },
  "models": {
    "WRFWeselySurfaceResistance": {
      "subsystems": {
        "dat": {
          "ref": "./wesely_data.esm"
        },
        "par": {
          "ref": "./wesely_parameters.esm"
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "igas": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 6.0,
          "description": "WRF gas index p_* (chem_opt = 101 numbering, 2 = so2, 6 = o3, 16 = nh3, ...) of each species on the axis. Selects the species constants and which of the four Rc paths applies, species by species.",
          "shape": [
            "spc"
          ]
        },
        "iland": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 2.0,
          "description": "USGS land-use category 1..25, WRF's `iland = luse2usgs(ivgtyp)`. NOT a Wesely 11-category index: the tables are pre-expanded over the USGS set."
        },
        "iseason": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 2.0,
          "description": "Seasonal category 1..5. wesely_driver produces only 1 (julday 90..270) or 2 for every non-MOZART mechanism."
        },
        "T": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "default": 288.0,
          "description": "Surface temperature, WRF's tsk(i,j)."
        },
        "rad": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "W/m^2",
          "default": 500.0,
          "description": "Net downward shortwave at the ground, WRF's gsw(i,j). Its being exactly zero is the day/night switch of the NH3 branch."
        },
        "rh": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "%",
          "default": 50.0,
          "description": "Near-surface relative humidity in percent, WRF's rhchem, clamped to [5, 100]. Only the SO2 branch reads it."
        },
        "wetflag": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "1 when the surface is dew-wetted (rhchem >= 95), else 0."
        },
        "rainflag": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "1 when it is raining (qr > 1e-18 or raincv > 0), else 0."
        },
        "highnh3": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "1 when chem(nh3) > 2 chem(so2), else 0. Read by the SO2 and NH3 wet branches."
        },
        "r_i": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "s/m",
          "description": "Minimum stomatal resistance for this land use and season."
        },
        "r_lu": {
